From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nouveau: keep GF117 DDR3 reclocking explicitly unsupported

GF117 RAMMAP 0x11/timing 0x20 sequencing is not validated. Reject every
GF117 RAM calculation before RAMFUC initialization so the PMU bootstrap
experiment cannot accidentally enter a memory transition.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/fb/ramgf100.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/fb/ramgf100.c
@@ -143,6 +143,10 @@
 	int N1, M1, P;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* GF117 DDR3 sequence is unverified; block before RAMFUC init. */
+	if (device->chipset == 0xd7)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	/* lookup memory config data relevant to the target frequency */
 	rammap.data = nvbios_rammapEm(bios, freq / 1000, &ver, &rammap.size,
 				      &cnt, &ramcfg.size, &cfg);
